<p>Jonny Cottrell, recently of <a href="https://www.yorku.ca/laps/phil/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">York University</a> in Toronto, and before that, the <a href="https://ppls.ed.ac.uk/philosophy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">University of Edinburgh</a>, has taken up a position at the <a href="https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">University of Toronto</a>.<span id="more-58265"></span></p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="wp-image-58266 aligncenter" src="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/cottrell-j-1024x979.png" alt="" width="418" height="400" srcset="https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/cottrell-j-1024x979.png 1024w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/cottrell-j-300x287.png 300w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/cottrell-j-768x734.png 768w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/cottrell-j-400x382.png 400w, https://dailynous.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/cottrell-j.png 1097w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 418px) 100vw, 418px" /></p>
<p><a href="https://www.jonnycottrell.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Professor Cottrell</a> works in the history of modern philosophy, with a focus on topics at the intersection of philosophy and psychology. You can learn more about his research <a href="https://www.jonnycottrell.com/research-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a> and <a href="https://philpeople.org/profiles/jonny-cottrell" target="_blank" rel="noopener">here</a>.</p>
<p>He took up his new position as associate professor of philosophy at the University of Toronto (Scarborough) this term.</p><p>The post <a href="https://dailynous.com/2026/09/01/cottrell-from-york-to-toronto/">Cottrell from York to Toronto</a> first appeared on <a href="https://dailynous.com">Daily Nous</a>.</p>